24:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"NL_OTEL_ENDPOINT"}]," builds one client-side load-balanced gRPC channel shared by\nall three exporters. Leave it unset and each exporter falls back to the\nOpenTelemetry SDK's own resolution: ",["$","code",null,{"children":"OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT"}]," (or the\nper-signal ",["$","code",null,{"children":"OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_METRICS_ENDPOINT"}]," and friends), defaulting\nto ",["$","code",null,{"children":"http://localhost:4317"}],". Both work; the explicit channel is what you want in\na cluster, because it re-resolves the collector's DNS as pods move. Either way\nthe transport is OTLP over gRPC: the binary is built with only the gRPC\nexporter, so ",["$","code",null,{"children":"OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL"}]," cannot switch it to HTTP."]}]
25:["$","p",null,{"children":"The rest of the surface is small enough to state in full:"}]
