77:["$","$L6a",null,{"value":"Direct to Prometheus","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":["Prometheus can receive OTLP itself (",["$","code",null,{"children":"--web.enable-otlp-receiver"}],"), but its\nreceiver is OTLP over HTTP at ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/api/v1/otlp/v1/metrics"}],", and Forge's\nexporters are built with the gRPC transport only. Setting\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL=http/protobuf"}]," does nothing, so there is no\nworking configuration that sends the binary's metrics straight into\nPrometheus. Something that speaks OTLP/gRPC has to sit in between; the\nshipped collector is that something, and its ",["$","code",null,{"children":"otlphttp/prometheus"}],"\nexporter is exactly this hop."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":["Read ",["$","$L1d",null,{"href":"#what-happens-if-you-skip-the-collector","children":"what happens if you skip the\ncollector"}]," before pointing the\nbinary at any OTLP/gRPC receiver other than the shipped collector: it\nrenames every metric."]}]]}]
